# workspaces: rules, a match and the wctl lines it applies to a window.
#
# The draw server reads this file at start and on a `reload` line to
# /srv/draw/ctl, from $home/lib/workspaces first and /lib/workspaces
# second, and applies each rule that matches when a window is named and
# when it says what program it is (`app` on wctl). A window no rule
# matches stays where it was born, on the current workspace.
#
# A match is terms, all of which must hold:
#   name=NAME      the window's name, exactly
#   title=PATTERN  its name, `*` any run
#   app=PROGRAM    the program, as `window` and the toolkit say it
#   first          no other window of its kind is up
#   transient      a window with a parent
# then wctl lines separated by commas. A name and a number is the old
# form, `name=` and `workspace`.
#
#   terminal              2
#   title=Debugger*       workspace 3, snap right
#   app=view first        snap grid 2 1 0
#   transient             raise
